{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>They shall not be eaten.</b> To hold liable the one who feeds them to minors — for thus it implies: they shall not be eaten through you. Or is it not rather to forbid them for benefit? Scripture says: ״לֹא תֹאכְלוּם״ — for eating they are forbidden, for benefit they are permitted. Every bird about which is stated לְמִינָהּ, לְמִינוֹ, לְמִינֵהוּ — in that species there are some that do not resemble one another, neither in appearance nor in names, and all are one species."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:48.863533327Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}